+Subject: [PATCH] fix: restore merge slot holder cleanup for crash recovery
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+The resolver implementation accidentally removed the encoded holder and
+stale slot cleanup mechanisms. This caused a vulnerability where a crashed
+orchestrator could leave the merge slot stuck, and the new run would
+timeout and proceed without the slot, risking concurrent merges.
+
+Restored:
+- SlotTimeout config option
+- slotHolders map for tracking encoded holders (taskID|PID|timestamp)
+- Encoded holder usage in acquireMergeSlot
+- Stale slot detection in waitForMergeSlot (checks for dead process or timeout)
+- Proper encoded holder release in releaseMergeSlot
+- cleanupStaleSlots() function for crash recovery on startup
+- cleanupStaleSlots() call at the start of Run()
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
